[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.7 Immediate extension semantics are missing]

No explicit extension unit is modeled.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.8 Shift source is incorrect]

MIPS immediate shifts operate on `rt`, but the source used is `Ain`, associated with `rs`.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.9 Load/store addressing is incorrect]

The model uses encoded register indices rather than register values in address calculation.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.10 Load writes into instruction register]

Load behavior modifies:

```text
IR[20:16]
```

rather than writing the loaded value to the register-file destination.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.11 Store writes register number rather than register content]

The store uses the instruction field, not the value read from the register file.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.12 No `$zero` protection]

Register zero can be overwritten.

[Section: 17. Critical Verilog / Datapath Problems > 17.16 Unused state/signals]

Observed unused or effectively unused elements include:
- `Regs`;
- `op`;
- `tree`.

